// This file is stored as "fips.go.hide" to hide it from "go mod" commands.
// Why? This is a weird edge-case of Go modules + optional boringcrypto
// compilation.
//
// "go mod" tries to ensure that all imported stdlib packages are present in
// GOROOT locally. The below "crypto/tls/fipsonly" package only exists on the
// dev.boringcrypto branch of Go:
// https://github.com/golang/go/tree/dev.boringcrypto/src/crypto/tls/fipsonly
//
// If you, fellow developer, didn't install Go locally from that branch, "go
// mod" will complain loudly (even though this file is not compiled due to the
// build tag at the top).
//
// So we have to "hide" this file from the "go mod" tools. Makefile in this
// repo will "unhide" the file (create fips.go->fips.go.hide symlink) when
// compiling in FIPS mode.
//
// If you have a better workaround idea, please suggest it!

package modules

// This import puts the crypto/tls package into FIPS mode.
import _ "crypto/tls/fipsonly"
